    (v_topic_id, 'A 43-year-old female with a history of breast cancer presents with a pathologic fracture of the proximal tibia. The lesion is lytic. What is the primary goal of orthopedic stabilization in this setting?', '["Curative resection of the tumor with wide margins", "Achieving a biologic union of the fracture site without cement", "Delaying surgery until radiation therapy is completed", "Immediate pain relief, early mobilization, and restoration of function", "Preventing pulmonary metastasis"]'::jsonb, 3, 'The treatment of metastatic pathologic fractures is generally palliative. The goals are to provide immediate mechanical stability (often using intramedullary nails and cement), relieve pain, and allow early weight-bearing and functional independence.'),
